    <summary>Windows Explorer right-click video downloader, converter, and media toolkit.</summary>

    <description><![CDATA[
## GFX Tools

GFX Tools adds a **"Paste link"** entry to the Windows Explorer right-click context menu.
Copy a video URL, right-click any folder, and click **Paste link** — the video downloads there.

### Features

- **Video download** from YouTube, Instagram, Pinterest, Facebook, and more (via yt-dlp)
- **Image download** from image galleries (via gallery-dl fallback)
- **Right-click context menu** integration — no app window to open
- **Advanced options** (Shift+Click): resolution cap, audio-only/video-only, audio format, time trimming
- **Convert to Compatible** — H.264 + AAC for NLE compatibility (right-click video files)
- **Compress** — HEVC for storage-efficient output (right-click video files)
- **GPU acceleration** — NVENC detected automatically, falls back to CPU
- **Adobe CEP plugin** for Premiere Pro / After Effects (download + auto-import)

### Requirements

- Windows 10/11 (x64)
- `yt-dlp` and `ffmpeg` — place in `%LOCALAPPDATA%\GFXTools\bin\` or on system PATH

### Install / Uninstall

The installer runs silently and registers the context menu entries for the current user only (no admin required).
`choco uninstall gfxtools` will cleanly remove all registry entries and the application directory.
    ]]></description>

